WEBVTT

00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:30.834
<v Speaker 1>Welcome to the 2006 World Championship Awards ceremony. Assisting me today in handing the trophies will be Yacht Brauer Level 5 judge from the Netherlands.</v>

00:00:31.724 --> 00:00:40.984
<v Speaker 1>Before we begin, I'd like to mention two awards that we've already presented. First in fourth place winning $15,000 from France Gabriel Nassif</v>

00:00:45.674 --> 00:00:50.944
<v Speaker 1>and in 3rd place winning $16,000 from Wales Nicholas Lovett.</v>

00:00:55.824 --> 00:01:06.104
<v Speaker 1>In the national team competition, the 2006 national team finalists winning a total of $15,000 from Japan Shohei Yamamoto,</v>

00:01:09.484 --> 00:01:11.134
<v Speaker 1>Hidenori Katayama</v>

00:01:13.494 --> 00:01:16.884
<v Speaker 1>and the Japanese national champion Cuts a Hero Mori.</v>

00:01:40.794 --> 00:01:50.424
<v Speaker 1>And now the 2006 national team champions, winning a total of $30,000 from the Netherlands. Julian Naughton,</v>

00:01:54.144 --> 00:01:55.844
<v Speaker 1>Robert Van Made Aborts</v>

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:02.634
<v Speaker 1>and the 2006 Dutch national champion Camille Cornelison.</v>

00:02:10.294 --> 00:02:15.484
<v Speaker 1>Once again the 2006 national team champions Team Netherlands.</v>

00:02:26.244 --> 00:02:32.964
<v Speaker 1>Please help me welcome the 2006 Pro Tour Rookie of the Year from Germany, Sebastian Tyler.</v>

00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:39.354
<v Speaker 1>Sebastian's not here. We'll get him as award later.</v>

00:02:40.424 --> 00:02:47.734
<v Speaker 1>And please help me welcome the 2006 Pro Tour Player of the Year from Japan, Shota Yasuoka.</v>

00:02:57.064 --> 00:03:02.954
<v Speaker 1>Once again, the 2006 Pro Tour Player of the Year, Shouta Yasuoka.</v>

00:03:09.704 --> 00:03:18.894
<v Speaker 1>And now the 2006 Magic the Gathering World Championship finalist, winning $25,000 from Japan Rio Ogura.</v>

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:44.944
<v Speaker 1>Ladies and gentlemen, the 2006 Magic the Gathering World Champion winning $50,000 from Japan, Mojito Mihara.</v>

00:03:53.024 --> 00:03:59.044
<v Speaker 1>Once again, your 2006 Magic the Gathering World Champion Mojito Mihara.</v>

00:04:08.604 --> 00:04:26.794
<v Speaker 1>I'd like to thank all the players, judges and staff that made the 2006 World Championships here in Paris such a great success. Please join us February 9th through 11th 2007 for the first Pro Tour of the 2007 season in Geneva, Switzerland. Thank you and goodnight.</v>

00:04:56.964 --> 00:04:58.494
<v Speaker 1>Tournament number 57.</v>

00:05:21.424 --> 00:05:22.054
<v Speaker 1>Pablo.</v>

